    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (73.76), both of whom benefit from prime matchups against favorable opposing starters. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is our standout play of the day; he draws Ethan Pecko, whose 5.95 xERA suggests a volatile outing, providing a +19% boost to our second baseman\u2019s efficiency score. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a high-leverage #2 spot in the order against Seth Lugo, whose 4.55 xERA creates a perfect environment for our slugger to drive in early runs. **Kyle Tucker** (71.13) also remains a must-start, as his ability to consistently contribute across all categories\u2014particularly his high-floor production against Bryce Elder\u2014keeps him firmly in the elite tier despite the slightly more difficult matchup conditions.\n\nManaging our game caps remains the primary concern as we navigate a roster heavy with \"Lineup Pending\" designations. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Sam Antonacci** (43.60); while he carries a solid profile for stolen base upside, the brutal matchup against Jacob deGrom\u2014a certified ace\u2014effectively capped his potential today. We opted to prioritize the power-platoon upside of **Heliot Ramos** (68.16) over the volatility **Sam Antonacci** would face against an elite arm. We are also keeping a close eye on the health of our depth, as **Andy Pages** remains on the IL, and we continue to monitor the statuses of **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Wade Meckler** to ensure we aren't burning starts on inactive players.\n\nRisk factors are elevated today due to the sheer volume of \"Lineup Pending\" tags, specifically regarding **Liam Hicks**, **Drake Baldwin**, and **Coby Mayo**. While **Liam Hicks** currently projections at 57.48, his score is highly sensitive to his placement in the #4 slot; should he drop down the order, we may need to pivot. Furthermore, **Jackson Merrill** faces a daunting task against Paul Skenes (3.17 xERA); while his base metrics keep him in the lineup, his proximity to the \"Below Floor\" threshold serves as a warning that we are banking on his raw talent over his matchup efficiency today.",
